{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_202605231817474a317547dc1d4b51","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-5.1","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_05629673d53b448ea803088b","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Fix cultivation factory bugs","prompt":"Fix the following bugs in D:/game-projects/steam-cultivation-factory/. Read each file before editing. Make targeted fixes only -- don't refactor.\n\n## Bug 1: Dual Realm Tracking desync (CRITICAL)\nFile: src/game/GameState.ts\nThe `addCultivation()` function updates `state.realm` but NOT `state.cultivation`. Fix it to update both.\nAlso fix `addCultivationToRealm` in src/renderer/App.ts to update both realm AND cultivation state.\n\n## Bug 2: Pill achievement tracking broken (CRITICAL)\nFile: src/renderer/App.ts\nThe `checkAchievements` call passes `pillsCrafted: {}` and `totalPillsCrafted: 0` hardcoded. Fix:\n- Add a tracking map `pillsCrafted: Record<string, number>` and counter `totalPillsCrafted: number` to the App class\n- When pills are successfully crafted (in the alchemy collection flow), increment the appropriate counters\n- Pass the tracked values to checkAchievements instead of empty values\n\n## Bug 3: Puppet state machine incomplete\nFile: src/game/Puppet.ts\nThe `tickPuppet` function advances progress to 1.0 but never transitions states. Fix:\n- When progress reaches 1.0, transition from 'idle' to 'picking' \n- When picking completes, transition to 'delivering'\n- When delivering completes, transition back to 'idle'\n- Set progress back to 0 on each transition\n- Call puppetPickup when transitioning from picking to delivering\n- Call puppetDeliver when transitioning from delivering to idle\n\n## Bug 4: Cross-region transfers duplicate resources\nFile: src/renderer/App.ts\nIn the cross-region link tick handler, resources are added but never deducted from source. Fix:\n- Before adding resources to destination, deduct the same amount from the state's resources\n- This simulates the transfer properly (since resources are global, deduct first then add back achieves the transfer)\n\n## Bug 5: Ascension multiplier not applied\nFile: src/renderer/App.ts  \nAfter a successful ascension, apply the 10x production multiplier. Add an `ascensionMultiplier` field to App class (default 1.0), set to 10.0 after ascension, and multiply it into the auto-production tick rates.\n\n## Bug 6: Talisman presets have wrong actions\nFile: src/game/Talisman.ts\nThe preset talisman `auto_stop_field` says \"stop the field when grass > 500\" but the action is `{ type: 'notify' }`. Change it to `{ type: 'stop_building' }`. Similarly fix any other presets that have wrong actions.\n\n## Bug 7: Conveyor glow color parsing\nFile: src/game/ConveyorBelt.ts\nThe glow effect uses `.replace(')', ',0.3)').replace('rgb', 'rgba')` which fails for hex colors. Fix:\n- If the color starts with '#', convert hex to rgba properly\n- Otherwise keep the existing rgb->rgba conversion\n\n## Bug 8: Camera event listener leak\nFile: src/renderer/Camera.ts\nAdd a `destroy()` method that removes all event listeners. Store the handler references so they can be removed. Use an AbortController for simplicity.\n\nMake all fixes. Do NOT change the overall architecture or add features. Only fix the listed bugs.","subagent_type":"general-purpose","run_in_background":true}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"561a5118-a4d0-464b-8f32-001690e29cb0","uuid":"73e19d12-66a1-44d7-81a7-ee8eb3c7e709"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_202605231817474a317547dc1d4b51","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-5.1","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_86e9e416ba124c2db844daa3","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Fix horror sim bugs","prompt":"Fix the following bugs in D:/game-projects/steam-horror-sim/. Read each file before editing. Make targeted fixes only -- don't refactor.\n\n## Bug 1: NPC behavior tree null reference (CRITICAL)\nFile: src/game/BehaviorTree.ts\nThe `createMysteriousCustomerTree(null!)`, `createLandlordTree(null!)`, and `createHimTree(null!)` all pass `null!` as the NPC parameter. The tree action closures reference `npc.state` which will crash.\n\nFix by refactoring the factory functions to return a function that takes the NPC and returns the tree:\n- Change each `createXxxTree(npc: HorrorNPC)` to return a factory that creates the tree with the actual NPC reference\n- In NPCManager constructor, create the tree AFTER the NPC instance is created\n- OR: Use a setter pattern where the tree's NPC reference is set after construction\n\nThe simplest fix: Make the factory functions accept an object with a `state` property, and pass the actual NPC after construction. Or use a lambda that captures the NPC from the manager's array.\n\nActually the simplest fix: In the factory functions, instead of closing over the `npc` parameter, close over a mutable reference holder `{ npc: null as HorrorNPC | null }`, then set the npc on it after construction. Like:\n\n```typescript\nfunction createMysteriousCustomerTree() {\n  const ref = { npc: null as HorrorNPC | null };\n  // build tree using ref.npc\n  return ref;\n}\n```\n\nThen after creating the NPC:\n```typescript\nconst ref = createMysteriousCustomerTree();\nconst npc = new HorrorNPC('mysterious_customer', ref.tree, ...);\nref.npc = npc;\n```\n\nOr even simpler: Just make the factory functions not take a parameter and instead return a tree that uses `this` bound context, or have the tree store a reference to its owner.\n\nSimplest approach: Make the factory functions take no NPC parameter and have them return tree nodes. In the NPC class tick method, pass `this` as context to the tree's tick. The tree actions should access the NPC through the context parameter of tick().\n\nLook at how the BehaviorTree tick() works and fix accordingly. The key issue is that closures capture `null!`. The fix must ensure the closures can access the actual NPC at runtime.\n\n## Bug 2: Customer stuck on anomalous transaction (HIGH)\nFile: src/game/CashRegister.ts\nIn `triggerAnomaly()`, after the timeout, `reset()` sets `currentCustomer = null` without finishing the customer. Fix:\n- Before setting `currentCustomer = null`, call `currentCustomer.finishCheckout(true)` or equivalent to un-stick the customer\n- Or call the customer's state change to make them leave\n\n## Bug 3: StoryManager acknowledgeEvent pushes undefined (HIGH)\nFile: src/game/StoryManager.ts\nIn `acknowledgeEvent()`, the event is filtered from `pendingEvents` first, then `find()` is called on the (now filtered) array. Fix:\n- Capture the event with `find()` BEFORE filtering\n- Then filter it out\n- Then push the captured event to storyLog\n\n## Bug 4: Player.toState() hardcoded zeros (MEDIUM)\nFile: src/game/Player.ts\n`toState()` returns hardcoded `money: 0, debt: 0, day: 1, health: 100, sanity: 100`. These should come from actual game state. Fix by accepting these values as parameters to `toState()` or from the App's state.\n\nActually, since Player doesn't own these values, the simplest fix is to mark them as optional in the return type or add a comment noting they're placeholder. But the best fix: Add parameters to toState() for these values.\n\n## Bug 5: NarrativeTypes typo (LOW)\nFile: src/game/NarrativeTypes.ts\nFix typo `'previous_clerck'` to `'previous_clerk'` in ClueCategory enum value. Make sure to check if any code references the old value and update those too.\n\n## Bug 6: Screen shake feedback artifacts (MEDIUM)\nFile: src/renderer/Renderer.ts\nThe screen shake uses `ctx.drawImage(ctx.canvas, shakeX, shakeY)` which draws the canvas onto itself. Fix by using `ctx.translate()` before rendering instead.\n\n## Bug 7: ProductManager expiry bug (MEDIUM)\nFile: src/game/ProductManager.ts\nWhen adding to existing inventory, the expiry date is not updated if the existing item already has one. Fix: when restocking, set the expiry to the NEW item's expiry (freshest stock determines shelf life).\n\n## Bug 8: Two competing save systems (MEDIUM)\nFiles: src/game/SaveManager.ts and src/game/GameState.ts\nBoth save to different localStorage keys. Fix by making SaveManager the single source of truth. Remove the save/load functions from GameState.ts that use a different key, and have App.ts only use SaveManager.\n\nMake all fixes. Do NOT change the overall architecture or add features beyond what's needed to fix these bugs.","subagent_type":"general-purpose","run_in_background":true}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"561a5118-a4d0-464b-8f32-001690e29cb0","uuid":"34091b30-8b89-4cc2-a2af-5dd4dbc8e7a7"}
{"type":"system","subtype":"task_started","task_id":"a84503f75963f89e0","tool_use_id":"call_05629673d53b448ea803088b","description":"Fix cultivation factory bugs","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_type":"local_agent","prompt":"Fix the following bugs in D:/game-projects/steam-cultivation-factory/. Read each file before editing. Make targeted fixes only -- don't refactor.\n\n## Bug 1: Dual Realm Tracking desync (CRITICAL)\nFile: src/game/GameState.ts\nThe `addCultivation()` function updates `state.realm` but NOT `state.cultivation`. Fix it to update both.\nAlso fix `addCultivationToRealm` in src/renderer/App.ts to update both realm AND cultivation state.\n\n## Bug 2: Pill achievement tracking broken (CRITICAL)\nFile: src/renderer/App.ts\nThe `checkAchievements` call passes `pillsCrafted: {}` and `totalPillsCrafted: 0` hardcoded. Fix:\n- Add a tracking map `pillsCrafted: Record<string, number>` and counter `totalPillsCrafted: number` to the App class\n- When pills are successfully crafted (in the alchemy collection flow), increment the appropriate counters\n- Pass the tracked values to checkAchievements instead of empty values\n\n## Bug 3: Puppet state machine incomplete\nFile: src/game/Puppet.ts\nThe `tickPuppet` function advances progress to 1.0 but never transitions states. Fix:\n- When progress reaches 1.0, transition from 'idle' to 'picking' \n- When picking completes, transition to 'delivering'\n- When delivering completes, transition back to 'idle'\n- Set progress back to 0 on each transition\n- Call puppetPickup when transitioning from picking to delivering\n- Call puppetDeliver when transitioning from delivering to idle\n\n## Bug 4: Cross-region transfers duplicate resources\nFile: src/renderer/App.ts\nIn the cross-region link tick handler, resources are added but never deducted from source. Fix:\n- Before adding resources to destination, deduct the same amount from the state's resources\n- This simulates the transfer properly (since resources are global, deduct first then add back achieves the transfer)\n\n## Bug 5: Ascension multiplier not applied\nFile: src/renderer/App.ts  \nAfter a successful ascension, apply the 10x production multiplier. Add an `ascensionMultiplier` field to App class (default 1.0), set to 10.0 after ascension, and multiply it into the auto-production tick rates.\n\n## Bug 6: Talisman presets have wrong actions\nFile: src/game/Talisman.ts\nThe preset talisman `auto_stop_field` says \"stop the field when grass > 500\" but the action is `{ type: 'notify' }`. Change it to `{ type: 'stop_building' }`. Similarly fix any other presets that have wrong actions.\n\n## Bug 7: Conveyor glow color parsing\nFile: src/game/ConveyorBelt.ts\nThe glow effect uses `.replace(')', ',0.3)').replace('rgb', 'rgba')` which fails for hex colors. Fix:\n- If the color starts with '#', convert hex to rgba properly\n- Otherwise keep the existing rgb->rgba conversion\n\n## Bug 8: Camera event listener leak\nFile: src/renderer/Camera.ts\nAdd a `destroy()` method that removes all event listeners. Store the handler references so they can be removed. Use an AbortController for simplicity.\n\nMake all fixes. Do NOT change the overall architecture or add features. Only fix the listed bugs.","uuid":"3e672d6d-45f4-4fd1-b91c-e8e3de0617ab","session_id":"561a5118-a4d0-464b-8f32-001690e29cb0"}
{"type":"system","subtype":"task_started","task_id":"a4a9481c1dfcc5ce1","tool_use_id":"call_86e9e416ba124c2db844daa3","description":"Fix horror sim bugs","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_type":"local_agent","prompt":"Fix the following bugs in D:/game-projects/steam-horror-sim/. Read each file before editing. Make targeted fixes only -- don't refactor.\n\n## Bug 1: NPC behavior tree null reference (CRITICAL)\nFile: src/game/BehaviorTree.ts\nThe `createMysteriousCustomerTree(null!)`, `createLandlordTree(null!)`, and `createHimTree(null!)` all pass `null!` as the NPC parameter. The tree action closures reference `npc.state` which will crash.\n\nFix by refactoring the factory functions to return a function that takes the NPC and returns the tree:\n- Change each `createXxxTree(npc: HorrorNPC)` to return a factory that creates the tree with the actual NPC reference\n- In NPCManager constructor, create the tree AFTER the NPC instance is created\n- OR: Use a setter pattern where the tree's NPC reference is set after construction\n\nThe simplest fix: Make the factory functions accept an object with a `state` property, and pass the actual NPC after construction. Or use a lambda that captures the NPC from the manager's array.\n\nActually the simplest fix: In the factory functions, instead of closing over the `npc` parameter, close over a mutable reference holder `{ npc: null as HorrorNPC | null }`, then set the npc on it after construction. Like:\n\n```typescript\nfunction createMysteriousCustomerTree() {\n  const ref = { npc: null as HorrorNPC | null };\n  // build tree using ref.npc\n  return ref;\n}\n```\n\nThen after creating the NPC:\n```typescript\nconst ref = createMysteriousCustomerTree();\nconst npc = new HorrorNPC('mysterious_customer', ref.tree, ...);\nref.npc = npc;\n```\n\nOr even simpler: Just make the factory functions not take a parameter and instead return a tree that uses `this` bound context, or have the tree store a reference to its owner.\n\nSimplest approach: Make the factory functions take no NPC parameter and have them return tree nodes. In the NPC class tick method, pass `this` as context to the tree's tick. The tree actions should access the NPC through the context parameter of tick().\n\nLook at how the BehaviorTree tick() works and fix accordingly. The key issue is that closures capture `null!`. The fix must ensure the closures can access the actual NPC at runtime.\n\n## Bug 2: Customer stuck on anomalous transaction (HIGH)\nFile: src/game/CashRegister.ts\nIn `triggerAnomaly()`, after the timeout, `reset()` sets `currentCustomer = null` without finishing the customer. Fix:\n- Before setting `currentCustomer = null`, call `currentCustomer.finishCheckout(true)` or equivalent to un-stick the customer\n- Or call the customer's state change to make them leave\n\n## Bug 3: StoryManager acknowledgeEvent pushes undefined (HIGH)\nFile: src/game/StoryManager.ts\nIn `acknowledgeEvent()`, the event is filtered from `pendingEvents` first, then `find()` is called on the (now filtered) array. Fix:\n- Capture the event with `find()` BEFORE filtering\n- Then filter it out\n- Then push the captured event to storyLog\n\n## Bug 4: Player.toState() hardcoded zeros (MEDIUM)\nFile: src/game/Player.ts\n`toState()` returns hardcoded `money: 0, debt: 0, day: 1, health: 100, sanity: 100`. These should come from actual game state. Fix by accepting these values as parameters to `toState()` or from the App's state.\n\nActually, since Player doesn't own these values, the simplest fix is to mark them as optional in the return type or add a comment noting they're placeholder. But the best fix: Add parameters to toState() for these values.\n\n## Bug 5: NarrativeTypes typo (LOW)\nFile: src/game/NarrativeTypes.ts\nFix typo `'previous_clerck'` to `'previous_clerk'` in ClueCategory enum value. Make sure to check if any code references the old value and update those too.\n\n## Bug 6: Screen shake feedback artifacts (MEDIUM)\nFile: src/renderer/Renderer.ts\nThe screen shake uses `ctx.drawImage(ctx.canvas, shakeX, shakeY)` which draws the canvas onto itself. Fix by using `ctx.translate()` before rendering instead.\n\n## Bug 7: ProductManager expiry bug (MEDIUM)\nFile: src/game/ProductManager.ts\nWhen adding to existing inventory, the expiry date is not updated if the existing item already has one. Fix: when restocking, set the expiry to the NEW item's expiry (freshest stock determines shelf life).\n\n## Bug 8: Two competing save systems (MEDIUM)\nFiles: src/game/SaveManager.ts and src/game/GameState.ts\nBoth save to different localStorage keys. Fix by making SaveManager the single source of truth. Remove the save/load functions from GameState.ts that use a different key, and have App.ts only use SaveManager.\n\nMake all fixes. Do NOT change the overall architecture or add features beyond what's needed to fix these bugs.","uuid":"561bc761-cd41-4232-91af-d4986223343b","session_id":"561a5118-a4d0-464b-8f32-001690e29cb0"}
